{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"fa7dac5c9164e910492037a9da4cc14a3bcbe81ade5571a26ce67b058592b496","digest":{"component_or_area":"terraform drift gating / infra CI","key_entities":[".github/workflows/terraform-drift.yml","infra/terraform/**","infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md","infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.review_interrupts","terraform plan -detailed-exitcode","Verified +1 gate","main branch"],"problem_keywords":["terraform drift","unapplied infrastructure","gerrit ci gate","plan drift detection","pre-submit verification"],"propositions":["Terraform drift workflow does not trigger on Gerrit changes, only on pull_request, push to main, or schedule, leaving no pre-submit verification that infra changes are applied before merge.","Un-applied terraform resources pass CI gates and land on main, triggering drift failures post-merge after Verified +1 was already granted, violating the assumption that green CI means the change is complete.","A terraform change touching infra/terraform/** can reach Verified +1 without surfacing whether its declared resources actually exist in the live infrastructure.","The manual terraform apply step is undocumented folklore rather than an explicit gating requirement or runbook attestation, making it easy to omit."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787705657306290001,"uuid":"d0006819-e9e7-465a-be8a-8b5c07806523"}